Some quick source-diving comes up with:

Death:
25% chance of no effect.
15% chance of insta-kill if not magic-resistant.
Otherwise, lose maximum HP (some fraction of the damage dealt):
		 * Apply some of the damage to permanent hit points:
		 *	polymorphed	    100% against poly'd hpmax
		 *	hpmax > 25*lvl	    100% against normal hpmax
		 *	hpmax > 10*lvl	50..100%
		 *	hpmax >  5*lvl	25..75%
		 *	otherwise	 0..50%
		 * Never reduces hpmax below 1 hit point per level.
If you're undead, no effect, but take normal damage.

Pestilence: Touch makes you sick, killing you in CON+d20 turns, or 
reduces time till death by two-thirds if already sick. No effect if 
sickness resistant.

Famine: Touch makes you lose 41 to 80 nutrition and abuses constitution.

If you're hit with a second attack in the same move, the second becomes 
a stun attack, for (damage) turns, but the damage you take is then halved.

The base damage for all rider touch attacks is 8d8.

All the riders are fire/cold/sleep/shock/poison/stone resistant. Death 
is also drain-life resistant.

If you try to teleport them, there's a 12/13 chance they'll end up next 
to you.

Best tactic is to stay away from them. Try to kill them from a distance. 
Keep some blessed potions of full healing on hand. Stunning is *bad*, 
especially since potions don't heal it, so keep a unicorn horn.

One unorthodox solution could be to polymorph into a ghoul (sickness 
resistant, drain life resistant, undead) and boost your HP with plenty 
of b!oFH, but being small they can't wear body armor, and probably need 
GoP to not be burdened.

